***REMOVED******REMOVED*** ✅ Type Usage Rules

***REMOVED******REMOVED******REMOVED*** 1. Shared Type Priority

**ALWAYS** use shared types instead of local interfaces:

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Use shared types
import type { BaseModalProps } from "../organisms/types";
import type { VoidCallback, AsyncCallback } from "../atoms/types";

interface ConfirmationModalProps extends BaseModalProps {
  onConfirm: AsyncCallback;
  onCancel: VoidCallback;
  confirmText?: string;
  cancelText?: string;
}

// ❌ FORBIDDEN - Local interfaces when shared types exist
interface LocalModalProps {
  isOpen: boolean; // BaseModalProps already exists
  onClose: () => void; // VoidCallback already exists
  title?: string; // BaseModalProps already has this
}
```

***REMOVED******REMOVED******REMOVED*** 2. Proper Type Extension

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Extend and refine shared types
interface MovieCardProps extends Omit<BaseCardProps, "variant"> {
  movie: Movie;
  onMovieUpdate: MovieUpdateCallback;
  variant?: "compact" | "detailed"; // Movie-specific variants
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Use generic shared types
interface SearchMoviesProps {
  onSearch: ChangeHandler<string>; // Instead of (query: string) => void
  onClear: VoidCallback; // Instead of () => void
}
```

***REMOVED******REMOVED******REMOVED*** 3. Callback Type Standardization

**MANDATORY** callback types to use:

```typescript
// From atoms/types.ts - ALWAYS use these
type VoidCallback = () => void;
type AsyncCallback = () => Promise<void>;
type ChangeHandler<T> = (value: T) => void;
type ErrorHandler = (error: Error) => void;

// Domain-specific callbacks
type MovieUpdateCallback = (movie: Movie) => void;
type UserActionCallback = (action: string) => Promise<void>;

// Usage in component props
interface ComponentProps {
  onSave: AsyncCallback; // ✅ Instead of () => Promise<void>
  onCancel: VoidCallback; // ✅ Instead of () => void
  onMovieUpdate: MovieUpdateCallback; // ✅ Instead of (movie: Movie) => void
  onError: ErrorHandler; // ✅ Instead of (error: Error) => void
}
```

